  "body": "### Which OS?\n\nWin10 Pro\n\n### Which release?\n\n22H2\n\n### Driver Version\n\n25.7.23、23.10.20.3\n\n### Device Specifications\n\nVDD and Sunshine run on a Qemu virtual machine with Windows 10 as the virtual machine operating system and Ubuntu 22.04 as the host operating system.\nCPU: 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i9-13900H\nGPU: Use the strongtz/i915-sriov-dkms project to virtualize the integrated graphics into multiple graphics cards, and bind one of the virtual graphics cards to the virtual machine for use.\nGPU Driver: Intel® Graphics Driver 32.0.101.6913 (WHQL Certified)\nSunshine: 0.23.1\n\n### Describe the bug\n\nSometimes, after successfully connecting to Sunshine, the error \"Terminating connection due to lack of video traffic\" is reported. After investigation, it was found that in this case, after the connection is successful, when Sunshine calls the AcquireNextFrame and ReleaseFrame interfaces of IDXGIOutputDuplication, it always returns the error DXGI_ERROR_ACCESS_LOST, resulting in the inability to capture the screen.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Compile the i915 driver according to the GitHub project strongtz/i915-sriov-dkms and copy the generated file i915.ko to `find /lib/modules/ -name \"i915.ko\"`.\n2. If the host machine does not have another graphics card, disable the integrated graphics card.\n3. SSH into the host machine and enable graphics card virtualization.\n4. Install the Qemu virtual machine, bind the virtual graphics card, and enable network connectivity.\n5. Install the Intel® Graphics Driver 32.0.101.6913, VDD 25.7.23, Sunshine 0.23.1, and QXL Driver in the virtual machine.\n6. Use Moonlight to connect to Sunshine (this issue will occur after connecting and closing the connection about 10 to 30 times).\n\nThis problem will not occur if you only change the operating system version to Windows 11 and keep other conditions unchanged.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n_No response_\n\n### Log File\n\n_No response_\n\n### Contact Details\n\n_No response_",
